# Architecture (analytics.admin)

List/detail shells know nothing about badges/metrics/stories. Entity-specific columns, filters, and form fields live in `entities/*`. Pages only compose. Do not build a generic `CrudResource` config.

## Entity slices (FSD)

Each slice in `entities/*` has segments `ui`, `model`, `api`, `lib` and a public `index.ts`. Pages import from the slice (`@/entities/badge`), not from files inside segments.

```
entities/badge/
  index.ts
  ui/          # Filters, FormFields
  model/       # zod schema, nuqs parsers
  lib/         # enum labels, table columns
  api/         # Orval re-export for this entity
```

## Forms

- `react-hook-form` + `zod` (`zodResolver`). Not `@mantine/form`.
- Fields are `Form*` wrappers in `shared/ui/form`: `name` + `control`, where `name` is `FieldPath<T>` from that `control`.
- Do not pass raw Mantine inputs into resource forms.

```tsx
<FormTextInput name="title" control={control} label="Title" />
```

## Filters

List filters are controlled `value` / `onChange`. Pages sync them to the URL with `nuqs` (`useQueryStates`). They are not RHF.

## Data

Pages call Orval hooks through the entity `api` segment, not from `CatalogPage` / `ResourceFormPage` / `DataTable`, and not via deep imports into `shared/api/generated`.
